From: StefanVonRanda <16295563+StefanVonRanda@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:19:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Load diffusers/PEFT, bare layers., legacy lora_unet_ and
 fused-qkv LoRAs

Upstream's apply_lora reads kohya keys only (diffusion_model.<module>.
lora_down/lora_up). The adapters this fork already loaded in 0.1.0 fail on
it: diffusers/PEFT files (transformer.<module>.lora_A/lora_B), MOSS Image
Edit's bare layers.N.proj.x.lora_A (no prefix, no .weight), sd-scripts'
legacy lora_unet_layers_N_proj_x (many ComfyUI LoRAs), and ai-toolkit's
fused layers.N.proj.qkv (paralaif's alpha LoRA), which MOSS's DiT keeps as
separate q, k, v.

- lora.py: load_lora groups any of those key forms by module path;
  apply_lora (upstream's: groups, per-module cast and pop, dtype) takes its
  modules from there; a qkv adapter on a block without qkv wraps q, k and v
  with the shared down and each one's third of up. Files without alpha use
  alpha = rank.

Checked: pytest 25 passed (each key form loads all 12 modules of a tiny DiT
and matches y = Wx + s * alpha/rank * up(down(x)); unknown keys rejected;
the qkv split equals the fused delta on CPU). All five adapter files on
this machine group into complete down/up modules; real renders with the
bare-key edit adapter and the fused-qkv alpha adapter: see the --reference
and --rgba commits.
Not checked: a real lora_unet_ file (none on this machine any more; the
format is covered by the unit test only).
